      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Studies were eligible if they assessed the gut microbiomes of human patients with AD or MCI with metagenomic sequencing and reported outcomes such as α -diversity, β -diversity ordination, relative abundances of various taxa, and linear discriminant analysis effect sizes (LEfSe). Eligible study designs were case-control and intervention studies (with baseline sampling). Patients had to meet well-defined diagnostic criteria such as DSM (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders) or NIA-AA (National Institute on Aging and Alzheimer's Association) guidelines.",
      "reason": "The text explicitly specifies study characteristics including population (AD/MCI), exposure (gut microbiome/metagenomics), outcomes (diversity, taxa), study designs (case-control, intervention), and diagnostic criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Wesearched MEDLINE, Scopus, EMBASE, EBSCO, and Cochrane for AD gut microbiome studies published between Jan 1, 2010 and Mar 31, 2022.",
      "reason": "Dissemination year is specified, but language and publication/report status criteria are not explicitly reported in the provided text."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "Reports excluded: Fungal microbiome (n=1) Non-NGS sequencing (n=5) Metagenomics not performed on AD group (n=2) Results not published yet (n=4) Samples from AD patients not demarcated (n=3) Uncontrolled pilot study (n=2)",
      "reason": "The PRISMA flow diagram text distinguishes exclusion reasons, listing 'Metagenomics not performed on AD group' (outcomes not measured) separately from 'Results not published yet' (results not reported)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "Twelve studies analyzed AD cohorts and ten studies analyzed MCI cohorts... All 17 included studies identify significant alterations in gut microbiome composition of AD or MCI patients compared to CN subjects.",
      "reason": "The text specifies the groups used in synthesis (AD, MCI, CN) and links them to the comparisons defined in the review objectives (AD/MCI vs CN)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "While eligibility criteria are listed, the text does not provide explicit rationales for notable restrictions (e.g., why metagenomic sequencing was required, why baseline sampling was required)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

